    "description": "Portland Natural Gas Transmission System is a FERC-regulated natural gas transmission pipeline serving New England and Atlantic Canada markets. Its customers include gas shippers, utilities, and power-market participants that rely on pipeline transportation capacity into the northeastern United States. The business is asset-heavy and contracted because value is tied to a long-lived interstate pipeline system and transportation agreements rather than commodity ownership. Company materials describe a 295-mile pipeline with approximately 460,000 dekatherms per day of capacity. Its principal operating corridor runs through New Hampshire, Maine, and Massachusetts, with connections into Québec and New Brunswick. TC Energy announced the sale of PNGTS in March 2024 to BlackRock's Diversified Infrastructure business and Morgan Stanley Infrastructure Partners, and public sources do not disclose the buyers' respective ownership percentages.",
