    "description": "Portland Natural Gas Transmission System is a standalone FERC-regulated natural-gas transmission business serving New England and Atlantic Canada. The approximately 295-mile system crosses New Hampshire, Maine and Massachusetts, connects with Canadian pipelines and has nearly 460,000 dekatherms per day of capacity. Its customers include utilities, energy marketers, industrial users and power generators. BlackRock- and Morgan Stanley Infrastructure Partners-managed funds announced the acquisition from TC Energy and Énergir on March 4, 2024 and closed it on August 15, 2024 for approximately US$1.14 billion including assumed notes. Regulatory evidence identifies BlackRock Global Infrastructure Fund IV and North Haven Infrastructure Partners III as equal 50% indirect owners through Beehive Loop AcquisitionCo LLC. The former owners' 61.7% and 38.3% direct interests ended at closing. PNGTS maintains a corporate office in Houston and an operating office in Lancaster, New Hampshire. No later company sale or signed pending exit was identified through August 23, 2026.",
